  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable Housing First for Ukrainian Recovery</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Housing First UA will provide immediate housing relief with a circular housing concept while at the same time establishing the capacity in Ukraine to rapidly produce and significantly scale up national production.Housing First UA will deliver turn-key houses for about 175 to 250 internally displaced persons (IDPs) in town of Oster in Chernihiv region. The houses are designed around a safe neighbourhood concept, with green spaces, children&apos;s playground, and a psychosocial center, all created by the project. Around twenty percent of Oster&apos;s population consists of IDPs.The houses are transformed from recycled shipping-containers to quality living spaces and are fully flexible. The production will be as much as possible implemented in Ukraine, by a team of Ukrainian skilled labourers trained by the project&#x2019;s key experts and on a production line that will be set up by the project partners.The lead partner, C3-Living, is the Netherlands modular housing producer and social-work organisation in one. The partner, Dobrobat, Ukraine&apos;s recovery non-governmental organisation (NGO), involved more than 50,000 volunteers to repair tens of thousands of homes since the start of the full-scale invasion in 2022.</narrative>
  </description>
